We will need significant amounts of additional new capital to fund the development of our GABAB PAM chronic cough drug candidate and our other drug programs and we cannot guarantee that we will have sufficient funds available in the future to develop and commercialize this indication or our other drug programs. As of December 31, 2025, we had cash and cash equivalents of CHF 1.6 million. To date, we have funded our operations through equity offerings, payments from licensors and divestment of selected assets. We have limited sources of revenue and will need substantial additional capital to develop and commercialize our drug candidates. We may be unable to raise additional capital when needed, or at all, which could force us to reduce or discontinue operations.
We believe that our current cash and cash equivalents are sufficient to fund our operating expenses through mid-June 2026. We cannot assure you of our ability to finance our operations and pursue our intended development plans beyond that date. Our ability to continue our operations will depend on our success in obtaining additional funding through existing and future partnership, grants, monetization of our intellectual property portfolio or our financial assets and additional fundings including equity offerings pursuant to our sale agreements with Kepler Cheuvreux and H.C Wainwright & Co. If our development plans are not successful, we may not be able to generate additional funding through partnerships or grants, or raise further financing through equity offerings or otherwise, or we may only be able to do so on terms that are not favorable to our shareholders.
